original_text:
Pléiades module scripts in engine/hypotheses/pleiades/prepare/:
- build_columns.py: per-impact columns, per stratum;
- hydro_sources.py: hydroacoustic source packages, named sources-<slug>-<constraint>.npz;
- rho_surface.py: correlated-error joint surfaces;
- rho_sensitivity.py;
- mixture_splithalf.py: three 4+4 partitions;
- speed_filter_report.py;
- redraw_core_b.py.
rerun_next.py takes --surfaces runs/pleiades/wide. It reads P(family) from EoF's p_core and maps exact EoF family keys (e.g. '00:19 R600 BTO Only +unpowered ~v212'), falling back to +alive. The 'independent misses' row is withdrawn until searched areas supplies its per-sensor Phase 2 layer.
